    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n673" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγλευκής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλεῦκος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not sweet, sour</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Hier.</u>
				1.21
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Rhinth.
				28
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλυκύς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				877b25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Lex.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			; heterocl. acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγλευκήν, θάλασσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					171
				</span></i>
			: metaph., of persons, <i>sour, crabbed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				140
			</span></i>; of the style of Thuc., <i>harsh</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Id.</u>
				2.12
			</span></i>, cf. [<i><span class="en">
				Longin.
			</span></i>]<i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				p.195
			</span></i> H.</div>
